\begin{abstract}
ASCE-RADEM v4.0 is a unified computational architecture integrating
exascale high-performance computing, post-quantum cryptographic telemetry
ingestion, and non-Euclidean geodesic optimal control. This dissertation
presents the mathematical foundations, system architecture, cryptographic
pipeline, control-theoretic framework, hardware implementation, and
experimental benchmarks demonstrating real-time atmospheric simulation
and control at 60\,Hz across 512 GPU compute nodes.
\end{abstract}

